# Known findings `make cve-scan` (Trivy) accepts, each with why it doesn't apply
# and a date by which it is reviewed again (Trivy reports it again after that
# date). Analysis: docs/security-review.md §4–5. Never add a finding here
# without that analysis.

# spring-webmvc 6.2.x: SSRF/RCE through XsltView. The app renders only
# Thymeleaf views and never uses XsltView. Fixed only in Spring Framework 7.x;
# goes away with the Spring Boot upgrade that brings it.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-01-31

# libssl3 (Ubuntu 22.04 base image): DTLS information disclosure. The JVM uses
# its own TLS stack, not the system OpenSSL, and the app speaks no DTLS. The
# fixed package isn't in eclipse-temurin:21-jre-jammy yet; `--pull` picks it
# up once it is.
CVE-2026-84782 exp:2026-11-30
